{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-jet-shell","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:jet-shell","kind":"remark","title":"Jet Shell of the universe","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-direct-limit-algebra"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-direct-limit-algebra","tags":["jet-shell","pro-finite","direct-limit"],"text":"jet-shell.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:jet-shell\"></a><p>In the limit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\to \\infty</code>, the infinite jet bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^\\infty E = \\varprojlim J^k E</code> becomes the <em>jet shell</em> of the universe. This pro-finite structure encodes all finite-level brane data. The algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_\\infty</code> (<a href=\"#def:direct-limit-algebra\">direct limit algebra</a>) acts on sections of the jet shell.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/jet-shell.md","heading":"Remark","number":"5.6.4"}
